<title>SLOVAKIA: DETAILS OF SLOVAK JANUARY CONSUMER INFLATION.</title>
<headline>DETAILS OF SLOVAK JANUARY CONSUMER INFLATION.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are details of</p>
<p>Slovak consumer inflation (CPI) for December, as released by</p>
<p>the Statistical Bureau (SUSR) on Wednesday.</p>
<p> SLOVAK CONSUMER INFLATION     Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>  pct change mo/mo		   1.1	0.3	 0.6</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		   5.8	5.3	 n/a</p>
<p>Foodstuffs, soft drinks</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   1.7	0.1	 0.7</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     5.4	4.4	 n/a</p>
<p>Leisure and culture</p>
<p> pct change month/month	    1.4	0.4	 6.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.1	9.1	 n/a</p>
<p>Hotels, cafes, restaurants</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   1.3	0.4	-0.9</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     7.7	5.3	 n/a</p>
<p>Transportation</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   1.0	0.3	 0.1</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     6.9	5.9	 n/a</p>
<p>Household, energy, utilities</p>
<p>and fuels</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.6	0.3	 0.3</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     5.4	5.1	 n/a</p>
<p>Alcohol, tobacco and</p>
<p>pharmaceuticals</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.8	0.3	 0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.2	3.9	 n/a</p>
<p>Furniture, household appliances</p>
<p>and maintenance</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.3	0.2	 0.0</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.3	4.0	 n/a</p>
<p>Education</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.9	0.2	-4.8</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    12.5	6.1	 n/a</p>
<p>Healthcare</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.4	0.1	-2.9</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	    11.1	7.4	 n/a</p>
<p>Clothes and shoes</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.6	0.7	 0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     7.2	7.0	 n/a</p>
<p>Various goods and services</p>
<p>  pct change month/month	   0.7	0.1	-0.4</p>
<p>  pct change year/year	     4.4	3.3	 n/a</p>
<p>Note: SUSR released the January monthly and yearly figures</p>
<p>on Tuesday.</p>
<p>SUSR said that due to the changes in the population's</p>
<p>expenditure structure, it had revised the formulas for</p>
<p>calcuating CPI, using 1995 data as a base.</p>
<p>The number of basket items has been cut to 708 from</p>
<p>previous 836. The new basket will have 11 main divisions and 38</p>
<p>groups. CPI indexes were previously published in four main</p>
<p>groups of items -- foodstuffs, non-food items, public catering,</p>
<p>services -- and 34 sub-groups.</p>
<p>SUSR did not release a comparative figure for a</p>
<p>year-on-year increase in January 1996 due to changes in</p>
<p>calculating the CPI. It also did not release revised figures</p>
<p>under the new formula.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
